          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மாலுமி — mālumi — \"a sailor\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மாலுமிகள் கப்பலைச் சுத்தம் செய்தார்கள். mālumikaḷ kappalaic cuttam ceytārkaḷ. The sailors cleaned the ship."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The plural is மாலுமிகள்."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மாலுமி (mālumi) is usually traced to Arabic muʿallim, \"a master, a ship's captain\"; the path into Tamil is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
